 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Classes supported on a map",
 "statement": "In the setting of [def-trf-correspondence-between-pairs], let\n$P\\in D(Z,A)$ and let $i:T\\to Z$ be a separated finite-type morphism of\nseparated finite-type $k$-schemes, with compact-support direct image\n$Ri_!$ as in the coefficient conventions. A *class supported on $i$*\nwith values in $P$ is an element of\n\n$$\nH_T^0(Z,P):=\\operatorname{Hom}_{D(Z,A)}\\bigl(Ri_!A_T,P\\bigr),\n$$\n\nwhere $A_T$ is the constant sheaf. The map $i$ is part of the data of\nthe class: it need not be an immersion, and different specified maps\nwith the same image give different groups.",
 "source": {
